<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - S.Africa Telkom yr attrib up 61 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - S.Africa Telkom yr attrib up 61 pct.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   up 61 pct to  1.9 bln rand</p>
<p>    Revenue		   up 23 pct to 16.3 bln rand</p>
<p>    Operating profit	up 46 pct to  4.4 bln rand</p>
<p>NOTE - Telecommunications utility Telkom has sold a 30 percent stake to a consortium of U.S.-based SBC Communications and Telekom Malaysia.  </p>
<p>    Shr (cts)		 50.0     vs 31.0</p>
<p>    Tax			 1.18 bln vs 0.42  bln</p>
<p>    Finance charges	 1.33 bln vs 1.43  bln</p>
<p>    Operating expenses   11.91 bln vs 10.29 bln</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said capital expenditure reached a record 3.7 billion rand during the year. It said it had connected more than 256,400 new working lines during the period -- up 71 percent from the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
